NeoMoM Antenna Modeling Suite
Authors and Contributors

==============================================================================
ORIGINAL AUTHOR
==============================================================================

John Shaeffer (KZ4TS)
North Fulton Amateur Radio League (NFARL)
Georgia, USA

  Creator of the NeoMoM project. Author of the Fortran computational
  engine, architect of the full suite, and designer of the GUI workflow,
  data formats, and visualization approach. AI tools were used to assist
  with Python GUI implementation under the author's direction and design.

==============================================================================
ACKNOWLEDGMENTS
==============================================================================

  NeoMoM builds on the foundational work of:

  - S. M. Rao, D. R. Wilton, and A. W. Glisson — whose 1982 paper
    defined the RWG basis functions used in the NeoMoM engine.

  - The developers of NEC (Numerical Electromagnetics Code) at Lawrence
    Livermore National Laboratory — whose code established the standard
    for wire MoM antenna analysis that NeoMoM was validated against.

  - Roy Lewallen (W7EL), author of EZNEC, whose work made antenna
    modeling accessible to the amateur radio community for decades.

  - The worldwide amateur radio community, whose enthusiasm for antenna
    experimentation and sharing motivates this work.

